# Every service builds with `context: .`, so without this file each of the
# ~50 image builds ships the entire repository to the Docker daemon —
# including 63 MB of `.git`. That is waste on a CI job that already needs
# an explicit `docker system prune` to fit, and it is a supply-chain
# surface: anything in the context is reachable by a `COPY`, and
# `vault-sync/Dockerfile` was doing exactly `COPY . .` until 2026-08-05.
#
# Every entry here was checked against the set of paths the Dockerfiles
# actually COPY (43 top-level paths). `check_dockerfile_context.py`
# enforces that permanently: a COPY source excluded by this file is a
# build that fails at `COPY`, and the gate reports it before the build
# does.

# Version control — the largest single item and the one that carries
# history, including anything ever committed and later removed.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Project management, docs and tests: never COPYed by any Dockerfile.
kai-pm
docs
scripts
tests
_archive

# Local environments and caches.
.venv
venv
node_modules
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
.coverage
.coverage.*

# Secrets and local configuration. Not COPYed, and must never be.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Editor and OS noise.
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
